    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Tetsuo: The Iron Man (1989) revolutionized cyberpunk horror with its feverish vision of technological infection. Director Shinya Tsukamoto created a nightmarish industrial wasteland where flesh melds with metal in grotesque ways, predating the body horror elements of <a href=\"/movie/837\" class=\"movie-title\">Videodrome</a> (1983) and <a href=\"/movie/473\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"473\">Pi</a> (1998). Shot in stark black and white with aggressive handheld camerawork and rapid-fire editing, Tetsuo's visual style influenced countless experimental films and music videos of the 1990s while establishing Tsukamoto as Japan's leading cyberpunk auteur."
      },
      {
